WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:00.850
<b>Host
Sakai Masato</b>

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.310
This time, we'll present one of Dazai Osamu's masterpieces.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:05.350
<i>Run, Melos!</i>

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.230
The defining work of Dazai Osamu's middle period, published in 1940

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.400
Run, Melos!

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.770
This work is actually

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:09.440
said to be based on Dazai's debt.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.740
Debt

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.530
Dazai managed to spend all of his money

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.490
by indulging with his fellow artist, Dan Kazuo,

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.790
at an inn in Atami.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.080
Dazai left Dan at the inn and went to his master, Ibuse Masuji,

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.670
to borrow money for the hotel charges.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.380
But several days passed and he didn't come back.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.220
Dan, who got tired of waiting, went to Ibuse's house.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.680
It turned out Dazai was unable to ask for a loan and was playing shogi with Ibuse.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.230
Dazai said to the angry Dan:

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:48.730
"My dear Dan, is it more painful to wait,

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.110
or to make someone wait?"

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:53.110
The masterpieces are blue.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.910
The
masterpieces
are blue

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.080
Please watch the first episode of <i>Run, Melos!</i>

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.540
May 1950

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.080
Is it more painful to wait?

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.670
Or to make someone wait?

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:26.140
Run, Melos!

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.610
One Month Ago

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:33.780
Yes?

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.940
It's the switchboard operator.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:35.900
Are you free to talk now?

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.660
Yeah, sure.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.370
Please wait.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:42.910
Takada?

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.450
Good morning.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.620
Ah, good morning.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.460
You were still sleeping, right?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:55.010
So, the play you wrote recently was really well-received.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.510
The place was packed,

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.090
and there were even standing guests on the final day.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:05.060
Well, that place isn't really big to begin with.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:05.600
Oh, come on.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.690
There's another job I'd like you to do.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.770
Yeah?

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:16.030
It's a Greek story compiled during the Roman times.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.320
It's quite the masterpiece.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.740
We're thinking of "Run, Melos!" as the title for it.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.160
"Run, Melos"?

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.120
We're already negotiating with the troupe.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.000
We'd like to start rehearsing as soon as the script is done.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:33.630
I see.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.090
The deadline is quite close though.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.880
But you always write so quickly.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.340
Is that so?

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.930
Yeah, it is.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.300
I'm sure it'll be popular.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.060
I wasn't interested in this job.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:56.530
I was reading that masterpiece in the train
on the way back. It was set in pre-era Sicily.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:01.490
Although it was eagerly recommended to me under the assumption I would like it,

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.530
I don't really get it.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.000
I don't really like stories about friendship.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.090
Still, I was quite pleased that I was asked to write this.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.430
It's not like anything else was worth my attention.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.770
Of course, I used to have something I wanted to write.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:34.060
But if you keep doing this kind of job,
such thoughts fade away by themselves.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.110
It's my distant past now.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.360
Having said that,

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.080
I don't consider myself an unhappy man.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.540
Of course, I'm not a happy man either.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:56.590
A happy man wouldn't write
plays and novels to begin with.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:05.590
I write while savoring my unhappiness. It's like I can taste it.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.270
Melos was...

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.770
Melos was enraged.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:19.230
He resolved to face that evil and tyrannical king.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.130
You would not even be able to kill a bug with such skill.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.340
I shall save the town with my own hands!

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.180
Yours?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.600
You are a hopeless man.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.850
You would not understand my loneliness.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:56.650
Don't say that!

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.400
Doubting people's hearts is a shameful vice!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.950
You are the ones who taught me that doubting is right!

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.870
People's hearts are unreliable.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.530
You can't believe them.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.080
You can't believe them...

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:33.020
Dionys imposed a death penalty upon Melos.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:37.270
And Melos said he was ready to accept it.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:43.110
However, he requested it be postponed for three days

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.860
so he could attend the marriage of his sister whom he had left in his hometown.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:48.700
Such a fool.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.870
What an outrageous lie.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:53.370
Would a bird come back once you let it free?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.500
Yes! I'll come back!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.460
I'll keep my promise.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.710
If you really don't believe me...

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:00.540
All right...

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.960
There is a stonemason named Selinuntius in this town.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.840
He is my only friend.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.840
Take him as a hostage here.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.640
If I don't come back here in three days by sunset,

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.720
please hang him!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.850
The king chuckled softly with cruel thoughts on his mind.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:21.560
He will most certainly not come back anyway.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:25.440
Therefore, it might be amusing to
pretend that I was cheated by that liar.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.200
Then it will feel nice to kill the substitute in three days.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.780
This is why you can't trust people.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:37.660
I'll put on a sad face and crucify the substitute.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:43.460
I'd love to show that to those who call themselves honest.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.850
Selinuntius was...

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.520
Selinuntius was summoned to the royal castle late at night.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:07.940
Forgive me, Selinuntius!

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.610
There is nothing to apologize for.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.410
Aren't we childhood friends?

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:12.990
Don't worry about it.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.450
No matter what happens, I believe in you.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.080
I thank you, my beloved friend!

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:26.170
I swear on Zeus' name that I, Melos,
will be back here in three days by sunset!

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.010
I know.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.420
I doubt you not.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:35.220
For the safety of your trip.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.290
I heard your wish.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.590
Come back here in three days by sunset.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:11.260
If you are late, I will kill your substitute.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.010
There's nothing wrong with coming a little late.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.390
I'll forgive your sin forever.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.600
What... What are you saying?!

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.180
I know it.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.730
If you value your life, come late!

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.770
I know your heart!

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.710
People's hearts are unreliable.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.260
You can't believe them.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.060
If you value your life, come late!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.440
I know your heart!

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:18.120
I know it...

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.620
Traitor!

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:32.920
Shit!

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:50.650
Yeah...

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:56.030
I used to have a dear friend in my hometown too.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:09:59.110
Only one.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.280
Run, Melos!
Only one.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:01.990
Run, Melos!

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:06.460
15 Years Ago

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:14.460
He jests at scars that never felt a wound.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:15.880
Wait.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.090
But, soft! What light through yonder window breaks?

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.220
It is the east.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.850
And Juliet is the Sun.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.640
Arise, fair sun,

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.690
and kill the envious moon.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.020
You are mine.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.440
My lover!

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.860
If only she could understand my heart...

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.990
Romeo, Romeo.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.870
Wherefore art thou, Romeo.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:46.290
Deny thy father and refuse thy name.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.670
And for that name which is no part of thee, take all myself.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:52.540
I take thee at thy word:

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:57.710
Call me but love,

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.630
and I'll be new baptized;

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.340
Henceforth I never will be Romeo.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.850
What man art thou that thus bescreen'd...

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:11.600
What man art thou that thus bescreen'd in night so stumblest on my counsel?

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.900
By a name, I know not how to tell thee who I am:

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:17.150
My name, dear saint, is hateful to myself, because it is an enemy to thee.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.690
I know the sound: Art thou not Romeo?

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:19.860
How camest thou hither, tell me, and wherefore?

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:24.070
With love's light wings did I o'er-perch these walls;

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.740
for stony limits cannot hold love out,

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:30.120
and what love can do that dares love attempt...

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:31.620
Hey!

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:37.380
"Hey" is for horses!

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.260
Would Juliet ever say that? You're a terrible actor.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.340
Give me a break!

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:44.260
I have no performance talent anyway.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.970
Talent, huh?

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:49.430
In that case, is our Takada's new work done yet?

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.980
Well, it doesn't matter anymore.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.020
Why not?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.150
I can't really write it well.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.820
It's impossible anyway.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.070
Because that show is...

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:02.910
Takada.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.370
You don't need to write well.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:08.870
Just write.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.750
Keep writing till the end.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.330
I don't want to read a good book.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.290
I want to read it because it's <i>your</i> book.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:21.970
Joshima!

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.220
That looks good on you!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.760
Amazing!

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.350
We don't have much at home besides clothing material.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:28.310
Romeo!

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.680
My Romeo!

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.150
We were friends.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.110
Although...

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:44.030
He was just so much more talented than me.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:48.830
Men like him have been favored by the heavens since birth.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:57.000
I was like one of the numerous planets that fly around the sun reaching for its light.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.550
A planet that reaches for the immaculate light of the sun.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.010
Not even the moon can shine by itself.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:10.600
It shines so brightly because it receives light from the sun.

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:24.110
How noisy!

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:44.210
You dumbass!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:51.890
Don't waste manuscripts!

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.390
Your hand is on fire!

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.690
It's hot!

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.200
Joshima!

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.790
I...

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.330
Impressive, Takada!

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.460
Congratulations, Takada!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:22.420
Congratulations!

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.800
Thank you!

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.760
I can't believe it.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.430
My work is being made into a show...

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:29.760
What are you saying?

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:30.970
Doesn't it make perfect sense?

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.400
Why?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.940
Why now?

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.740
It was fifteen years ago.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:55.410
I buried both his words and smile into the depths of my memories,

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.830
and started living alone in Tokyo.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:04.880
I managed to fill the crevice in my heart by
continuing to fill the squares on my manuscript paper.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:06.550
And yet...

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:11.930
I feel my chest swelling up with pain again.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:15.010
It stings my heart like a fresh wound.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:20.100
How long does he have to make me suffer before he's satisfied?

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:21.230
Shit!

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.240
Brother!

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.320
Welcome home, Brother!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.490
I'm home.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:32.530
I'm glad.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:35.200
I was worried since you were quite late.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:35.830
Sorry.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.330
Did something happen, Brother?

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.250
No.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:39.870
Nothing.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.000
You lie!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.290
Something happened, right?

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.840
I'm not gonna be a child forever.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.920
I still have some important things to do in the town.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.300
Let's have your wedding tomorrow.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:49.800
Tomorrow?

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.130
The sooner the better.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:53.300
Also...

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.010
I bought you a wedding dress.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:57.430
Great!

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:58.890
Thank you, Brother!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:06.610
Now hurry up and tell everyone in the village.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:07.770
Yeah, yeah.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.490
Brother, I'll shout and tell everyone!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.920
Be blessed by the goddess Artemis.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:28.380
We shall make the vow of marriage here today.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.850
Congratulations!

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.020
Congratulations on your marriage.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:43.190
Thank you, Brother.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:44.390
Don't cry.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:47.190
Tears don't look good on a happy bride.

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:50.190
I have to go now.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:51.780
I have important things to do.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:58.240
What your brother hates the most is doubting and lying.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.950
You know that, right?

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:02.950
I'll leave my sister in your hands.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:04.500
Okay!

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.460
And now for the feast!

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:17.260
People merrily clapped their hands, sang and danced.

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:20.140
The feast became more and more flashy.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:23.230
I want to stay here forever.

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:26.310
I want to spend my life with these good people.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:30.570
Melos still felt attached to his life.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.400
But that feeling wouldn't get the better of him.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.340
Here it is.

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:33.960
Hey, Joshima.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:38.010
Jeez.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:39.680
I laughed so hard I started crying.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.140
Were you crying?

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.100
Takada.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.150
I'm going to Tokyo.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.730
I'm leaving my home.

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.280
I don't want to live at home anymore.

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:01.740
Will you go with me?

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.240
Let's do theater together in Tokyo.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.960
You'll write and I'll perform.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:29.390
His father ran a big used clothing store in his hometown.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:32.440
That used clothing store also lent people money.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:36.150
He was like the town magnate.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.280
As the only child,

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:41.660
I think Joshima had an argument with his father about his future career

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.990
and decided to go to Tokyo.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:49.870
As soon as I heard his words,
I made up my mind immediately.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.870
If he goes, I'll go too.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.790
There was no wonder or doubt in my mind.

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:58.590
The train comes at ten.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:19:59.760
Wait for me.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:03.260
But I don't have a watch with me.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.050
I see.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.140
Take this.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:14.020
People can say anything pure with their mouths.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:19.070
I can see their true motives.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:23.780
I'll prove to the king that you can believe in people!

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.370
Then I'll laugh as he crucifies me!

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:35.210
The harshest snow of winter came on the day we were to go to Tokyo.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:39.460
Even though I was freezing under my flannel coat,

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:43.760
there was a warm pulsation in my chest I had never felt before.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:48.720
I felt like I could go anywhere with him.

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.680
Be it heaven or hell.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:55.150
Or the end of the world with no one else in sight.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.940
I shall be killed tonight.

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.570
I shall run to get killed!

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.950
I shall run to rescue my friend! My substitute!

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.620
I shall run to defeat the deception and trickery of the king!

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.540
I must run!

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:11.830
Farewell, dear hometown!

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:12.100
I'll prove that you can believe in people!

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:23.230
That's... an utter lie.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:30.010
Finale
Next Time
Run, Melos!
